From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: KYTY_FEWER_TRAPS streams small buffers outside
 GPU-shared memory again

Patch 0033 turned the stream path off whenever GPU-shared memory is on. Memory
that cannot be shared (no linear backing, or off a shared page boundary) then
went back to write-watching: in DREDGE about 135 buffers a frame were synced
and write-protected again by the GPU thread (mprotect was 18% of it), and the
game threads took about 300 write faults a frame. With KYTY_FEWER_TRAPS set,
small read-only buffers in such memory stream again (copied at each use, not
protected); shared memory is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
index 0e39d5d1e7ca980441243621ad00b31a0a9bd758..bfec2348bf2f37ba4689991d0c6d44c8b233b08d 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cinttypes>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <string>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <memory>
 #include <utility>
@@ -585,9 +586,23 @@ std::pair<Buffer*, uint64_t> BufferCache::ObtainBuffer(uint64_t vaddr, uint64_t
 	EXIT_IF(!(GuestRange {vaddr, size}.Valid()));
 
 	static const uint64_t stream_max = EnvSize("KYTY_STREAM_MAX_KB", 1024, 256 * 1024);
-	if (m_direct_page == 0 && !is_written && size <= stream_max &&
+	// KYTY_FEWER_TRAPS: with GPU-shared memory on, memory that cannot be shared (no linear
+	// backing, or not on a shared page boundary) still streams, as it did before: a small
+	// buffer the CPU rewrites every frame is copied at each use instead of being write-protected
+	// again after every sync (DREDGE: about 135 protects and 300 write faults a frame).
+	static const bool fewer_traps = [] {
+		const char* value = std::getenv("KYTY_FEWER_TRAPS");
+		return value != nullptr && *value != '\0' && std::string(value) != "0";
+	}();
+	const auto can_be_direct = [&] {
+		uint64_t backing = 0;
+		return LibKernel::Memory::GetLinearBacking(vaddr, size, &backing) &&
+		       (vaddr - backing) % m_direct_page == 0;
+	};
+	if (!is_written && size <= stream_max && (m_direct_page == 0 || fewer_traps) &&
 	    !m_memory_tracker.IsRegionGpuModified(vaddr, size) &&
-	    m_memory_tracker.IsRegionCpuModified(vaddr, size)) {
+	    m_memory_tracker.IsRegionCpuModified(vaddr, size) &&
+	    (m_direct_page == 0 || !can_be_direct())) {
 		// Within one draw window the guest has no signal to rewrite the range. A copy made in this
 		// tick at most an eighth of a lap ago is nearly a lap ahead of the ring's writes, like a
 		// fresh copy, even if the draw's preparation submits the tick.
